{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>You shall not take, etc.</b> The explanation is: because an oath declares the greatness and sovereignty of HaShem, a person might think that if he swears by His name, blessed be He, it is for honor and glory, for this is his Master and Sovereign — even if it is for nothing (lashav), what of it, if the one who swears to Him does not recognize his falsehood, for if he knows that He is this man's master, and it is in a manner where the opposite will not be revealed? Therefore He said <b>you shall not take</b> — even if there is sovereignty in the Name by which you swear, <b>for HaShem will not absolve</b> even if his intention is to bear His name, since it is for nothing (lashav)." "<b>Further,</b> it intends that through the medium of a false oath he bears aloft from upon himself the Name of HaShem that is called upon him, and clothes himself in the aspect of evil that is associated with a false name, for the Name of HaShem is truth, and one who mentions it in falsehood — the aspect of the Name departs from him because of his having chosen emptiness (shav). And this is the reading of the verse: <b>you shall not take</b> upon yourself <b>the Name of HaShem your Elohim</b> for the cause of emptiness, and He said <b>for HaShem will not absolve</b> those who do so." "<b>Further,</b> it alludes that one should not bear upon himself the Name of HaShem — that He is his Elohim — and say to all that he is a Jewish man and a servant of HaShem, when this is what it says — <b>the Name of HaShem</b> which is <b>your Elohim</b> — but his heart does not think thus, and this is what it says <b>for nothing (lashav)</b>. And this is a warning not to deceive [others] by saying that he is among His servants when he is not so. And included in this warning is that one should not present himself as more righteous than he is."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:30:53.565412301Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}